Description: Fix CVE-2026-45383 out-of-bounds read in decode_slice_unit_WPP
 During WPP (wavefront parallel processing) slice decoding, ctbAddrRS is
 recalculated each loop iteration without validation; when it grows too
 large, the subsequent array access pps.CtbAddrRStoTS[ctbAddrRS] reads past
 the end of the allocated vector. The existing guard only validates
 slice_segment_address, not the ctbAddrRS values computed during the loop.
 This adds a bounds check on the CTB row range against the picture height
 before entering the WPP entry-point loop, rejecting crafted WPP HEVC images
 with DE265_WARNING_SLICEHEADER_INVALID.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/commit/d1a2c3b4b751d21f44e8e82220fe9766c9d116ff
Author: Dirk Farin <dirk.farin@gmail.com>
Last-Update: 2026-07-18

--- a/libde265/decctx.cc
+++ b/libde265/decctx.cc
@@ -1016,6 +1016,10 @@
   int ctbAddrRS = shdr->slice_segment_address;
   int ctbRow    = ctbAddrRS / ctbsWidth;

+  if (ctbRow + nRows > img->get_sps().PicHeightInCtbsY) {
+    return DE265_WARNING_SLICEHEADER_INVALID;
+  }
+
   for (int entryPt=0;entryPt<nRows;entryPt++) {
